   419	## 7. FG composition
   420	
   421	_Round 5 (async session) supplied the forms below. The exact final
   422	statements of (A) and (B) come from r147 and blueprint-opus; they enter
   423	the catalog as versioned entries and do not change this structure._
   424	
   425	### 7.1 Decisions (user, 2026-09-28)
   426	
   427	- The FG is fixed: our Simplex FG (the DC §7 finality gadget, without SG,
   428	  grades or safe votes). Its definitions are in LM; its lemmas are proved
   429	  once in `Kit.FG`.
   430	- APs vary. An AP plugs in by proving the AP-side entries.
   431	- FG heights never skip.
   432	- Every height pair (target or timeout) needs the AP's certified source;
   433	  with no source the pair is empty (certified pairs).
   434	- **Interference is relative to a height.** If height h* ends up
   435	  finalized (even before this is known), then from h* + 1 there is no FG
   436	  interference: the root can still change (the J at h* is revealed), but
   437	  every valid block of height > h* extends F*, so the change only prunes
   438	  branches that never reached h* + 1. The NJ arm (m = H + 1) and the
   439	  finalized arm (m = h* + 1) are two cases of "no interference from
   440	  height m". A fixed filter is only a special case.
   441	- Fallback: an AP that cannot meet the AP-side entries is certified
   442	  white-box as one composite instance.
   443	
   444	### 7.2 Interface
   445	
   446	**Anchor function (LM).** `anchorsOf : View → Block × Finset Block`
   447	returns `(F, anchors)` for a duty view V_d.
   448	- `View` is defined formally: the processed blocks of the duty's frozen
   449	  view (the frozen HEAD view, the full proposal view), closed under the
   450	  F evidence basis (the accepting carrier, the J carrier, a descendant
   451	  witness; r143 §2.1). The basis stays in every duty view across the
   452	  F-advance cut, so F stays viable in frozen views.
   453	- It is evaluated at duty time on the duty's own view (R1). R1 is a
   454	  DELIBERATE DEVIATION from DC, which reads live control caches (audit
   455	  M04; fgsa-fast.md). The correspondence theorem is proved for the
   456	  duty-view version.
   457	- `anchors` = the viable entries at FG height h_max − 1 above the root;
   458	  {J} when the root is J (h_max = h_j + 1); {genesis} while h_max = 1.
   459	- Correspondence theorem (`Kit.FG`, versioned): DC's viable set in V_d
   460	  equals the blocks on root–anchor paths plus anchor descendants in V_d,
   461	  under the entry invariants, the admission rule, the F-advance cut and
   462	  frozen branches. Two orders stay apart: in the chain transition,
   463	  finality comes before height; the store update changes h_max, then J,
   464	  then F.
   465	- `process` does only FG admission (F ⪯ B) for the choice tree.
   466	
   467	**AP facets.** `FGTarget` (the height-pair source body), `FinalityHead`
   468	(the DC finality pair comes from the AP head at the action, not from
   469	`FGTarget`), `AnchorChoice` (only the HEAD and proposal walks read the
   470	anchors; other AP rules may use the raw tree), and row inclusion.
   471	
   472	**HavocFG (LM).** A FAMILY of composites `AP ⊗ HavocFG σ`, indexed by the
   473	honest FG signing rule σ (which may equivocate). The FG transition,
   474	admission, `anchorsOf` and the payload format are fixed. AP-side
   475	certificates are uniform: one proof for every σ. `Kit.Compose`
   476	instantiates σ with the Simplex rule. FG-internal claims (accountable
   477	safety, honest never slashable) stay in `Kit.FG`.
   478	
   479	### 7.3 AP-side conditions and entries
   480	
   481	All quantifiers range over honest duties d with time t_d in the interval.
   482	Every control value is computed from the duty's own view V_d.
   483	
   484	Conditions (L1, observable in `AP ⊗ HavocFG σ`):
   485	
   486	- `Settled [t₀, t₁)`: F_d is constant; the root of the anchor set is
   487	  constant; the UNION of all honest anchor sets in the interval is an
   488	  antichain. With the band fixed, anchor sets only grow: new branches at
   489	  the same entry level may enter a view, and that is not a change. The
   490	  settling bound is t₀ = (the last effective change) + P, the relay of the
   491	  maximizing witness into every freeze (r146 §5.1). Used by (B).
   492	- `Retains (X, u) [t₀, t₁)`: for every block B in the explicit set X,
   493	  every honest duty at a time ≥ max(u_B, t₀) has an anchor comparable
   494	  with B, so B is in its allowed tree. For (A), X = the honest
   495	  `FGTarget` source BODIES named at duties ≥ u (not only their entries).
   496	  X is explicit, so there is no vacuous exception.
   497	- `ArmedRetained B [b₀, b₁] := Retains ({B}, b₀) [b₀, b₁]`: indexed by the
   498	  armed prefix. It replaces v4's `ProtectedCompatible`, which is false in
   499	  Outage (X and Y can both descend the armed B).
   500	
   501	Entries:
   502	
   503	```text
   504	┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   505	│ Entry                │ Statement (form; exact text from r147)         │
   506	├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   507	│ ap.floored           │ F ⪯ every AP output at every honest read,      │
   508	│                      │ outside a node's rejoin interval               │
   509	│ ap.anchorCompliant   │ the head, the finality head and the target     │
   510	│                      │ descend the chosen anchor                      │
   511	│ ap.includesRows      │ every honest proposal includes every FG row    │
   512	│                      │ received before its inclusion cutoff           │
   513	│ ap.honestSourced     │ an honest FGTarget has an honest supporter     │
   514	│                      │ that held it as Protected at its own cutoff;   │
   515	│                      │ same-round honest targets are compatible       │
   516	│                      │ (local, not a public certificate)              │
   517	│ ap.targetSafe (A)    │ under Retains of the target bodies: I1–I3      │
   518	│ ap.targetLive (B)    │ after GST, under Settled for ρ: one common     │
   519	│                      │ target at the honest action, and it advances   │
   520	│ ap.armedSafe         │ the AP's safety, inclusion and P1 claims under │
   521	│                      │ ArmedRetained, in clean and Outage regimes     │
   522	│ ap.outputRecovered   │ under Retains of all target bodies from the    │
   523	│                      │ reset on: every exposed output is safe and     │
   524	│                      │ monotone within ρ_out, and contains every      │
   525	│                      │ later honest proposal within its delay         │
   526	│ ap.finalityHead      │ in an honest opening-plus-two-slots window,    │
   527	│                      │ the current-slot finality head is the slot-1   │
   528	│                      │ proposal and descends the anchor               │
   529	└──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   530	```
   531	
   532	`ρ` and `ρ_out` are conclusion parameters; they may depend on
   533	participation (r146).
   534	
   535	### 7.4 FG-module lemmas (`Kit.FG`)
   536	
   537	- **Provenance laws (audit B05).**
   538	  - (P1) Height-source provenance: an honest height pair (h, T) at
   539	    action a has a source body C = that duty's `FGTarget`, with
   540	    σ[C].h = h. An empty `FGTarget` gives an empty height pair.
   541	  - (P2) Entry extraction: T = σ[C].T_h, immutable in the parent state,
   542	    so T ⪯ C and h(T) = h(C). The history invariant keeps C, not only T
   543	    (r146 §4, "retain source bodies").
   544	  - (P3) Finality provenance: an honest finality pair names the latest J
   545	    of the finality head. That J is justified by an earlier target
   546	    quorum; since q > a, it has an honest target row with its own
   547	    (P1)/(P2) provenance. A finality pair can be nonempty when
   548	    `FGTarget` is empty; its harmlessness reduces to that of the earlier
   549	    justification.
   550	- **(C) Harmless.** Every J, carrier or F whose quorum contains an honest
   551	  row keeps `Retains` for every source body that the row's provenance
   552	  names. The carrier case uses the r143 band lemma (§5.1): T ⪯ B implies
   553	  h(B) ≥ m, else B ⪯ Q.
   554	- **HeightRetains (m).** Every block of state height ≥ m in V_d that
   555	  descends F_start is in the allowed tree of d. `Kit.FG` converts it to
   556	  `Retains` for the AP's targets at heights ≥ m.
   557	- **(D) Causal cap.** At the causal cut, old honest row heights are ≤ M;
   558	  old-only crossings can reach M + 1.
   559	- **(E) Base selection, two arms.** Both discharge `HeightRetains (m)`:
   560	  the NJ arm with m = H + 1 (NJ holds in the selected event prefix, not
   561	  forever), and the finalized arm with m = h* + 1 (the actual F*, its
   562	  crossing properties, a separate source-history argument).
   563	- **(F) Certified pairs** give the first NJ + 1 transfer. The later
   564	  history is the source-body induction (§7.5).
   565	- **FG-internal.** Accountable safety, honest never slashable (durable Λ),
   566	  finalized monotone (durable F).
   567	
   568	### 7.5 Composition (`Kit.Compose`)
   569	
   570	**Induction (audit M05).** Invariant at event e: every honest `FGTarget`
   571	and every source body signed before e is retained by every honest duty
   572	up to e. Step lemma: a HEAD at q_s reads only rows emitted at actions
   573	≤ d_(s−1), and q_s < d_s. So a row emitted at d_s cannot justify or move
   574	the band of any HEAD at or before q_s. The source transfer at q_s uses
   575	only earlier objects (r146 §3.2). Regimes are used in bounded-prefix
   576	form (§4).
   577	
   578	**Joint recovery: nine steps (audit B06).**
   579	
   580	```text
   581	┌───┬──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────┐
   582	│ # │ Step                         │ Owner                               │
   583	├───┼──────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┤
   584	│ 1 │ settle views at a fixed      │ Kit.FG (relay of the maximizing     │
   585	│   │ frontier                     │ witness)                            │
   586	│ 2 │ bound effective root changes │ Kit.FG (unique J at m−1 under a≤f;  │
   587	│   │ at the frontier              │ F changes)                          │
   588	│ 3 │ repair interval without      │ Kit.Compose, from 1–2 and           │
   589	│   │ global AP recovery           │ ap.targetLive under Settled         │
   590	│ 4 │ matching, nonempty progress  │ ap.targetLive (common target) +     │
   591	│   │ rows                         │ Kit.FG (matching rows; no in-band   │
   592	│   │                              │ lock elsewhere)                     │
   593	│ 5 │ mature carriers, height rise │ ap.includesRows + proposer          │
   594	│   │                              │ recurrence + Kit.FG transition      │
   595	│ 6 │ select the NJ or finalized   │ Kit.FG (E), in the selected event   │
   596	│   │ base                         │ prefix                              │
   597	│ 7 │ first-source transfer and    │ ap.targetSafe under Retains +       │
   598	│   │ later source bodies          │ Kit.FG (P1–P3, band, root gap) +    │
   599	│   │                              │ the induction above                 │
   600	│ 8 │ recover the ordinary AP      │ ap.outputRecovered                  │
   601	│   │ outputs                      │                                     │
   602	│ 9 │ finality head and strong     │ ap.finalityHead + Kit.FG finality   │
   603	│   │ recurrence                   │ kernel                              │
   604	└───┴──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┘
   605	```
   606	
   607	**Explicit FG liveness premises.** FG quorums by identity (full
   608	participation or q honest awake after GST) and
   609	`StrongMultiProposerRecurrence` (DC) as a named condition; full
   610	participation alone gives no proposer windows.
   611	
   612	**Clean and Outage regimes.** The AP claims carry over under
   613	`ArmedRetained` and the induction above.
   614	
   615	**Restart (M02).** On restart, available drops to F; so available
   616	monotonicity and inclusion exclude a node's rejoin interval (joiner
   617	semantics). h_max and J need not be durable: they are derived again from
   618	the chain states of received blocks.
