     1	# FG-SA: conditional safety, conditional progress, and finite filter changes
     2	
     3	_2026-09-28. Rule authority: [Astra §§2–4](fgsa-fast.md) and
     4	[Opus §2](fgsa-fast-opus.md). Plain SA; DC finality; no SG and no PC._
     5	
     6	**PROVED** below means a paper proof from the stated execution premises.
     7	It does not mean a new Lean theorem. **SKETCH** means an incomplete proof;
     8	**REFUTED** means a false statement; **OPEN** means no proof or refutation
     9	here. The changes to the SA walk require the explicit arguments below.
    10	Neither existing Lean executable is the FG-SA executable.
    11	
    12	The conditional results are (S) in §3 and (L) in §5. They do not assume
    13	that the base has already recovered. The only extra FG condition in (S)
    14	is the filter condition N2. In (L) it is N1. The execution, delivery,
    15	participation, and proposer premises are listed in §1. The proof that NJ
