    33	
    34	## 1. Premises and clocks
    35	
    36	Use a valid, reachable FG-SA execution, starting with the specified
    37	initial state. An arbitrary pre-GST execution is permitted. Arbitrary
    38	independently assigned S records, leases, or Λ records are not permitted.
    39	There are n base seats per label and n unit-weight FG identities, as in
    40	the two rule documents. The same static faulty set has size a. Counts
    41	at different base labels are never added.
    42	
    43	```text
    44	h = n−a;             f = (n−1) div 3;
    45	τ = (n+1) div 2;     q_F = (2n+2) div 3;
    46	a ≤ f;              h ≥ q_F ≥ τ;       h > 2a;
    47	2q_F−n > a;         τ > a.
    48	
    49	Δ > 0; k ≥ 2;       L = (4k−1)Δ;
    50	t_s = 4sΔ;          v_s = t_s+Δ;
    51	e_s = t_s+2Δ;       z_s = t_s+3Δ;
    52	q_s = t_s+5Δ;       d_s = t_s+6Δ;
    53	P = 4RΔ; R ≥ 3;     T_r = rP; a_r = T_r+6Δ = d_(rR);
    54	δ_t = 2R slots;     ρ = 2L+G+8Δ;
    55	σ = (g+3)P+G+6Δ;   B_static = ρ+2σ.
    56	```
    57	
    58	The following premises apply through every time used in a conclusion.
    59	
    60	1. All honest validators participate after GST. Each has one HEAD per
    61	   scheduled label and one FG action per scheduled round. They process
    62	   clocks and receipts as specified. Honest identities do not equivocate.
    63	2. Post-GST messages and accepted complete dependencies have strict Δ
    64	   delivery and relay. The return-relay condition covers objects already
    65	   accepted at GST. An emission is not a receipt, even at the sender.
    66	3. Blocks and signatures are authentic. Parents have smaller slots.
    67	   Roots identify blocks uniquely. Views have the specified ancestor
    68	   closure. Original declared support subsets remain unchanged. A later
    69	   path receipt does not convert a raw-only declaration into support.
    70	4. For (L), an awake honest proposal occurs strictly after each relevant
    71	   trigger and within G. Also use Rec(g): every inclusive round window
    72	   `[r,r+g]` contains an honest opening whose next two **slot** proposers
    73	   are honest. Use the rule documents' `g≥3`. The full window and every
    74	   gate used must fit in the horizon. Strong recurrence for first finality
    75	   is not used here. Neither K nor the debt parameter D enters (L).
    76	5. Honest proposals include the specified current-window rows from the
    77	   pool and from held current-window blocks, except rows already on the
    78	   parent chain. Use `w_F≥1`, full-row deduplication, and distinct FG
    79	   identities. A faulty carrier may use old authentic rows. Stored
    80	   progress bits persist until that chain advances height.
    81	6. The source at action r is exactly the deepest member of
    82	   `FastWrite_i[rR] ∩ D_action` with a live deadline. An empty latest gate
    83	   does not fall back to an earlier gate. Targets, repeats, and timeouts
    84	   all use this source. The finality pair instead uses the actual full-view
    85	   finality head. Its own finality pair overrides the lock at the same
    86	   height before the height-pair branch is evaluated. Λ persists.
    87	7. R1 is used at every duty. Gates, saved raw results, resolution, and
    88	   release remain unfiltered. The whole-result S guard tests all live
    89	   leases, including excluded leases. Only a successful guarded gate
    90	   writes S and leases. Finality does not assign to S.
    91	
    92	For (S), a synchronous source label means that its complete SA delivery,
    93	return-relay, and late-test premises hold. `t_s≥GST` is a sufficient
    94	condition. The claim is not based on `a_r≥GST` alone. The proof needs the
    95	same receipt properties at each later label it uses. The SA definition
    96	`SynchronousLabel` explicitly includes execution, delivery, relay, honest
    97	majority, and horizon conditions [SA1].
    98	
    99	Full participation and `a≤f` are retained throughout this document to
   100	match the recovery job. The source-to-HEAD part of (S) can use weaker
   101	majority premises. No such weakening is needed for this interface.
   102	
   103	## 2. Two precise meanings of no FG interference
   104	
   105	For each honest duty d, take its own R1 view V_d. Compute its controls
   106	together, as in the rule documents:
   107	
   108	```text
   109	F_d = current accepted F, with its retained acceptance basis;
   110	H_d = max({1} ∪ {h(W) : W∈V_d});
   111	(j_d,J_d) = greatest justified pair in V_d compatible with F_d;
   112	Z_d = J_d if H_d=j_d+1, else F_d;
   113	
   114	D_d = {B∈V_d : F_d⪯B, Z_d⪯B,
   115	                  ∃W∈V_d, B⪯W and h(W)≥H_d−1}.
   116	
   117	Ret_d(B) := B⪯Z_d
   118	            or (Z_d⪯B and B∈D_d).
   119	```
   120	
   121	The first arm of Ret allows the root to move past B along B's chain.
   122	It is therefore weaker than requiring B to remain a member of D_d.
   123	The second arm requires a band witness in **this** view. Compatibility
   124	with F and Z alone is insufficient. Ancestor closure supplies the path
   125	from Z_d to B in this arm.
   126	
   127	**N1(u,v;m,F,Z): static controls.** At every honest proposal, HEAD, and
   128	FG choice duty in `[u,v]`, `H_d=m`, `F_d=F`, and `Z_d=Z`. R1 and the
   129	retained-F-basis rule continue to hold. Each duty computes D_d from its
   130	own view. The full archival honest frontier is m until the stopping
   131	event under consideration. Views, block sets, scores, leases, and raw
   132	results need not be equal. New blocks and band witnesses may arrive.
   133	The unused lower justified pair need not be fixed when Z=F.
   134	
   135	N1 concerns the selection rule, not literal equality of D_d. This matters:
   136	the honest proposal itself must enter later views. A static filter may
   137	also exclude an old lease target below the band. No claim that all old
   138	protected blocks remain eligible is part of N1.
