   240	## 3. Base proof: close the exact-choice and pending-gate gaps
   241	
   242	### 3.1 The certificate and walk facts
   243	
   244	Every progress or target QC contains an honest height row since `q_F>a`.
   245	Its entry T is a prefix of its successful fast source C. Each such C
   246	has an honest supporter since `τ>a`. Finality names an already justified
   247	entry and thus has this earlier target origin.
   248	
   249	For a duty view of maximum `m+1`, take the first height-`m+1` carrier Q
   250	on a maximizing path. The view contains Q and its height-m entry T.
   251	If its honest source C is compatible with a protected B, then T and B
   252	are comparable. If `T⪯B`, B has height at least m. If `B≺T`, Q is a
   253	height-`m+1` witness above B in this very view. Therefore B is viable
   254	when above F. If F already extends B, the floor contains B instead.
   255	This proof uses the view's own maximum, not a maximum from another read.
   256	
   257	The SA forward and reverse relay count is unchanged. For a genuine
   258	prefix B, surviving support makes its edge strictly better than each
   259	conflicting sibling. A source with support at least τ also releases all
   260	conflicting leases at q_s. These are the two different parts of
   261	`fast_source_permanent_support`. Domain membership must be supplied
   262	before using the score part. Extra below-band eligibility does not
   263	defeat a strict score comparison on a retained path.
   264	
   265	### 3.2 The healthy induction
   266	
   267	Induct on base labels. At a label retain these facts for all earlier
   268	raw genuine results, including results whose writes were vetoed:
   269	
   270	1. Each earlier genuine prefix is covered by all subsequent healthy
   271	   HEAD batches and by the corresponding honest proposal parent.
   272	2. Each lease has an earlier genuine origin. Every earlier FG source
   273	   has such an origin, with its actual source body retained.
   274	3. Each required path is in the duty domain, or its root extends that
   275	   path's protected prefix.
   276	4. The signed proposal merge preserves the actual selected suffix and
   277	   gives exact adoption of an honest current proposal.
   278	
   279	Genesis supplies the initial case. At q_s an FG row that can already
   280	control a carrier has an earlier action than d_s. Its source label is
   281	therefore at most s−1. The inductive history, followed by the certificate
   282	fact in §3.1, supplies the root and band premises for the next transfer.
   283	The new row at d_s cannot prove, or change, the earlier HEAD at q_s.
   284	
   285	At a current genuine result, a branch conflicting with any retained old
   286	genuine prefix has only faulty support. Let b be the number of faulty
   287	participants at that label. Its support is at most b, whereas the late
   288	pool has at least `h+b` participants and `h>b`. It cannot pass the strict
   289	majority. Hence the new result is compatible with all older lease
   290	origins and FG source bodies. The guard and the S update preserve the
   291	single chain. The transfer count then supplies item 1 at the next HEAD.
   292	
   293	Here is the missing exact-proposal comparison. Let P be an honest
   294	proposal in slot u and A its selected parent. At its same-slot HEAD,
   295	no lease can have an origin later than label u−2: the label-(u−1)
   296	gate is still pending. By the preceding induction, every such target
   297	precedes A. Each already emitted FG source also has label at most u−2.
   298	Its transfer HEAD is no later than `t_u−3Δ`. The previous-label batch
   299	used by the proposer therefore covers that source. Every controlling
   300	checkpoint entry precedes A.
   301	
   302	This parent assertion does not assume exact proposal adoption. First
   303	apply the carrier lemma to the full proposal view for each older
   304	genuine origin. All controlling source origins are compatible by the
   305	preceding label's induction. The root is compatible, and the previous
   306	batch's strict score reaches each retained origin from a start below
   307	it. A start above it already contains it. Thus the composed proposal
   308	parent covers these origins before the HEAD comparison begins.
   309	
   310	Take a maximizing carrier at either read. The honest source of its last
   311	crossing is one of those earlier sources. Its entry T precedes A, so
   312	`h(A)≥h(T)=H_read−1`. This remains true when a late F basis makes the
   313	HEAD maximum greater than the proposal maximum. Thus A, P, and their
   314	needed paths are viable at both reads. A root or a lease start at either
   315	read lies on the same path to A.
   316	
   317	Compare the walks edge by edge:
   318	
   319	- Frozen votes and resolved support relay to the proposer before t_u.
   320	  P returns the proposer's raw set and original support subset. The
   321	  two score functions therefore agree on the compared paths.
   322	- Frozen block paths and declared support paths were available at the
   323	  proposer. Extra lease paths precede A and cannot add a competitor
   324	  above A or beside the selected suffix.
   325	- An extra F-basis path adds no support key. An edge on such a path
   326	  with a non-equivocating declared supporter already has its complete
   327	  path in the declared-support arm. A genuinely new unsupported edge
   328	  has only the common equivocation score.
   329	- If an old edge becomes eligible only because the HEAD has a larger
   330	  band threshold, its parent is below that threshold. The maximizing
   331	  carrier's entry T is below A and has the transferred previous-label
   332	  honest support. At a divergence before reaching that threshold, the
   333	  edge toward T strictly beats the new edge. At or above the threshold,
   334	  the below-band exception does not apply.
   335	- At A there is no eligible old child that can defeat P. Such a child
   336	  with ordinary eligibility would already have defeated the proposer's
   337	  stopping choice, by the same scores and path transport. Also
   338	  `h(A)≥H_HEAD−1`, so the HEAD cannot enable it by the band exception.
   339	  P is the only current-slot proposal, is eligible, and has no valid
   340	  same-slot descendant.
   341	
   342	Therefore the actual HEAD is exactly P. This replaces Opus's false
   343	set-inclusion shortcut that the entire voter view is a subset of the
   344	proposer's view plus P. A late F basis need not satisfy that inclusion.
   345	The proof needs equality of the relevant comparisons, not equality or
   346	inclusion of the whole views. It also replaces the claim that the two
   347	walks have the same start: an FG root can move the start along the
   348	already selected path without changing the result.
   349	
   350	The pending label-(u−1) gate at `t_u+2Δ` cannot add a conflicting lease.
   351	Its raw genuine result has transferred to the HEAD at `t_u+Δ`, which
   352	was just shown to be P. Its slot is earlier than P's slot, so it is a
   353	prefix of P. At `t_u+6Δ`, the exact honest P batch has
   354	`2h>h+b`. It gives P at every genuine read; the guard passes. Older S
   355	cannot be a strict descendant of this new P. Thus every S contains P
   356	at +6Δ. This closes the pending-gate clause without assuming that the
   357	pending lease was already present at the HEAD.
   358	
   359	This induction uses `a<h`, not `a≤f` and not FG quorum turnout. It
   360	proves clean safety, monotonicity, and 6Δ service. F and S remain on
   361	the same chain. The accessor is their greater prefix and is monotone.
   362	The changed proof follows the origin/root/parent/HEAD/guard order in
   363	`CleanInclusion.lean`; it does not instantiate that theorem on a
   364	different executable `Run`.
   365	
   366	### 3.3 The outage boundary
   367	
   368	Let B be in a clean S at `T=d_s`. Put `j=max{u:e_u≤b₀}`. For slow P1,
   369	
   370	```text
   371	b₀≥T+L−3Δ  implies j≥s+k;
   372	e_j=d_(j−1)≤b₀<d_j=e_(j+1).
   373	```
   374	
   375	The k healthy batches ending at j contain B. The pending gate d_j
   376	therefore writes B everywhere with deadline `d_j+L>b₀+L`.
   377	For fast P1, use lag 4Δ and `h_t≥τ` throughout the healthy prefix.
   378	That gives the same pending write by the fast test.
   379	
   380	Before d_j, the retained healthy batch and the exact pending-duty step
   381	above protect the HEAD at q_j. There is no intermediate FG action
   382	strictly between e_j and d_j; an action at d_j follows the gate.
   383	Old rows use the healthy source history. Before a first later departing
   384	HEAD, every new honest fast source is compatible with B: an incompatible
   385	source could have at most a supporters. The same-view carrier proof
   386	then prevents a first domain exclusion. If the root is below B, the
   387	live B lease is effective; if it is above B, it already contains B.
   388	
   389	Release has at most a conflicts, below τ. Expiry is after b₁. A new
   390	conflicting S write fails the guard; an ancestor result keeps S. Finality
   391	has a compatible target origin and cannot remove B at the accessor.
   392	Both P1 claims follow with `Π=min(η,L)` and the original lags.
   393	
   394	## 4. Reset history: close Lemma R
   395	
   396	Use the actual named base from the DC causal construction. Write x for
   397	its predecessor height. In the NJ arm, x=H and the retained event prefix
   398	has no honest target or lock at H. In the finalized arm, use its actual
   399	checkpoint F* at height x, not an assumed NJ bit. The source label of
   400	the least honest height-(x+1) row is wholly after GST. These are base
   401	premises established by the arrival construction in §5, not premises
   402	about an arbitrary multiple of K.
   403	
   404	Let r* be that least round, s*=r*R, C* its source body, and T* its entry.
   405	
   406	**First transfer.** An honest surviving supporter held the complete C*
   407	path at v_s*. Relay puts that path in every freeze z_s*. No earlier
   408	honest row at x+1 exists, so no earlier carrier at x+2 can exist.
   409	Each q_s* view has maximum exactly x+1. The NJ record induction excludes
   410	J at x in this prefix. In the finalized arm, any J at x equals F*;
   411	every block above height x extends F* by DC's finalized-crossing law.
   412	In either case the root is below C*. The path is viable. The τ release
   413	removes every conflicting lease, and the strict score transfer makes
   414	every q_s* HEAD cover C*. Same-label genuine compatibility excludes a
   415	conflicting pending write at d_s*.
   416	
   417	Now strengthen Opus's induction as follows. Retain the finite chain of
   418	**all** honest selected source bodies since the first source round.
   419	For each body B in this chain retain its start time q_s and these clauses:
   420	
   421	```text
   422	(i)   Every honest HEAD from q_s contains B.
   423	(ii)  Every surviving lease at those release reads is compatible with B.
   424	(iii) B's path remains in every later frozen view unless F extends B.
   425	(iv)  Every later honest selected source is compatible with B.
   426	(v)   Every row at B's height names B's immutable height entry.
   427	```
   428	
   429	Induct on slots, adding the sources of an action round together. This
   430	avoids an arbitrary order between honest actions at the same tick.
   431	Their genuine results are compatible, so the deepest source in that
   432	round supplies a common source path for the whole group.
   433	
   434	**Lagging HEAD views.** Once a source B has transferred, its complete
   435	path was received before its first freeze and is in every later frozen
   436	view. Therefore that view's maximum is at least h(B); it cannot lag
   437	below h(B). If its maximum increases, use its own maximizing carrier.
   438	For a crossing supported before r*, the entry height is at most x.
   439	B extends C* and has height at least x+1, so this old crossing cannot
   440	remove B by the band. An old J below x is inactive at a maximum at
   441	least x+1. An old J at x is absent in the NJ prefix, or is F* in the
   442	finalized arm.
   443	
   444	For a crossing supported at or after r*, use the source body of its
   445	honest row. If that source preceded B's label, the honest supporter of
   446	B covered it by the induction. If it was at B's label, same-label
   447	compatibility applies. If it followed B's label, its honest supporter
   448	covered B before the proposed first departure. In all cases the source
   449	is compatible with B. Section 3.1 gives viability using the carrier in
   450	the current view. The identical argument gives compatibility of J and
   451	F with B. A root above B is sufficient; a root below B permits the path.
   452	No equality between a full-read maximum and a HEAD maximum is used.
   453	
   454	**Actual choice and pending deeper leases.** At the first transfer of B,
   455	fast release removed every conflicting lease, including excluded leases.
   456	At that label's pending gate, all genuine results are compatible with
   457	the source result. A deeper new lease K that is compatible with B is
   458	either below B or extends B. Its start therefore cannot bypass B.
   459	Subsequent honest batches all cover B. Their strict majority prevents
   460	new conflicting genuine results, including results saved under a veto.
   461	Lease expiry and release only remove starts. The retained B path and
   462	strict score comparison then reach B from every remaining start below
   463	it. This is exactly the `origin`, `same`, `preserve`, and `transfer`
   464	induction in `source_support_induction`, with the domain premise now
   465	proved separately for each call.
   466	
   467	At a new action, a source incompatible with an earlier retained body
   468	would have only faulty supporters, fewer than τ. It cannot be selected.
   469	For the new source's first transfer, all already used controlling rows
   470	are earlier than that transfer HEAD. The previous paragraph therefore
   471	supplies its compatible historical origins without using its new row.
   472	Add this source and repeat. This proves (i)–(iv) for all later time.
   473	
   474	The NJ premise is needed only for the old rows in the starting prefix.
   475	Do not assert that every possible later state at H remains NJ forever.
   476	Later signatures at H are covered by the same new-source history; a
   477	later finality change cannot introduce an old conflicting target origin.
   478	
   479	**Named entries and successors.** Let T be the first named entry at
   480	height y≥x+1. Every later source at y is compatible with the first source
   481	at y. Compatible blocks at the same height have the same entry, by the
   482	immutable plateau rule. Thus every such row names T, whether target or
   483	timeout. At the least row at y+1, the new source contains T. Its new
   484	entry T' also contains T: T' cannot be a proper ancestor of T, since
   485	`h(T')=y+1>y=h(T)` and height is monotone on a path.
   486	
   487	Consequently every old target root at predecessor height y is exactly
   488	T and lies below T'. This is the missing named-predecessor clause in
   489	`frame_succ_main`. Source-body coverage proves it; compatibility with
   490	C* alone would not. The two callbacks in that DC proof are supplied:
   491	same-round witness equality and later source/entry compatibility.
   492	The SG fields in its current record still need a new FG-SA record in
   493	Lean, but no grade is needed in this paper proof.
   494	
   495	**The finalized arm.** The proof above uses `finalized_preceq_of_height_lt`
   496	and same-height justified-entry uniqueness where the NJ arm uses the
   497	no-target-at-H record induction. Those are precisely the separate
   498	`floor`, `rootBelow`, and `sourceAbove` clauses constructed in
   499	`namedHeightRegimeFrame_of_finalizedRun`. A finalized ancestor alone
   500	does not order its descendants; the fast-release and source-body
   501	induction supplies that order. Thus the finalized arm has the same
   502	permanent history, without a timer or an NJ predecessor.
   503	
   504	Finally the next honest batch after each source transfer has h supporters
   505	above that body. At its gate, every genuine result covers it and no
   506	conflicting lease survives. Hence every S contains it by
   507	`d_(s+1)=t_s+10Δ`. This proves delayed inclusion, not inclusion at a_r.
   508	
   509	## 5. Recovery budget and the limit of the shorter argument
