   944	
   945	The mismatches and their effect on the composition are these.
   946	
   947	**M1 — (L) under literal N1.** r147 §6 itself proves that an F advance
   948	below the band excludes no band branch. It states that a uniform count
   949	"would require continuation of exact service through lower F advances".
   950	The trunk lemma (§4.1) gives this continuation for a fixed view: the walk
   951	results and the band sources are unchanged. Two places in r147 §4 read
   952	the fixed F. (a) Admission of the honest witness A: A has height ≥ m−1 >
   953	h(F′), so A extends every new F′ (F4). (b) The accepted-F basis arm of the
   954	R1 HEAD view: a new F′ basis can reach a HEAD view before it reaches the
   955	proposer. Its blocks carry no declared support. Above the band they are
   956	not eligible. Below the band, an edge on them is eligible but has score
   957	0 (plus the common equivocation count), which the supported path's
   958	strict majority defeats. This is the third bullet of
   959	[fgsa-adjudicate §3.2](fgsa-adjudicate.md). With (a) and (b), r147's (L)
   960	holds under the effective N1 with the same λ. A line-by-line re-proof of
   961	r147 §4 under the effective N1 is not written here. Therefore H16 is
   962	SKETCH. Without H16, use §9.4.
   963	
   964	**M2 — (S) scope.** r147's (S) covers the source of an honest nonempty
   965	height row. That is enough for Theorem N and H-FG: Lemma C and Lemma K
   966	use only row sources, and C* is a row source (H17). Theorem H needs more
   967	(H18):
   968	
   969	- (S) for fast bodies at every synchronous label. r147 §3's proof reads
   970	  only the fast count, release, the pending gate, and the S guard; it
   971	  never uses the fact that the label is an action label.
   972	- (S_slow). r147 §4 proves slow-source support inside a static interval.
   973	  After NJ the filter is not static; the needed form replaces N1 by keep
   974	  of the slow body, with the same expiry step (`d_(s−k)+L = q_s`).
   975	- (S2). r147 N2 already includes proposal duties. The proposer's walk
   976	  uses the label-(u−1) frozen votes, which all cover B by (S1); the same
   977	  strict-score transfer then puts B on the proposer's path.
   978	
   979	Each item has a proof route in r147's own arguments, but none is stated
   980	there. H18 stays OPEN until they are.

