     3	_2026-09-27. Paper scope. Integer counts. The C* authentication gap is explicit._
     4	
     5	**Build FG-PC-SA first.** Use SA-PC as the available chain. Start with an
     6	FFG candidate that freezes its source, preserves mandatory SA leases, and
     7	forms a fresh PC checkpoint after a recovery interval. Do not start by
     8	replacing PCs with justifications. Do not claim that the r19 bound transfers
     9	by addition of the SA recovery time. The joint protocol still needs a proof.
    10	
    11	```text
    12	┌──────┬─────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    13	│ Item │ Status  │ Finding                                              │
    14	├──────┼─────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    15	│ 1    │ PROVED  │ An FFG link and a TA PC certify different facts.     │
    16	│      │ REFUTED │ Delete the PC test from r19 without a replacement.   │
    17	│      │ OPEN    │ A smaller FG-SA with a proved transfer rule.         │
    18	│ 2    │ PROVED  │ Base recovery bound: 2L+G+8Δ, with stated premises.  │
    19	│      │ REFUTED │ Use the old r19 deadline on the unchanged SA base.   │
    20	│      │ OPEN    │ Joint recovery and base P1 for the new composition.  │
    21	│ 3    │ SKETCH  │ One available output; additive strong and FG claims. │
    22	│      │ OPEN    │ FG accountability in the strict anonymous C* engine. │
    23	│ 4    │ SKETCH  │ Frozen source, mandatory leases, later PC target.    │
    24	│      │ OPEN    │ Full proof and the best epoch/recovery constants.    │
    25	└──────┴─────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    26	```
    27	
    28	PROVED identifies an existing theorem or a paper implication with explicit
    29	premises. It does not mean that the new full protocol has a Lean proof.
    30	REFUTED identifies a specific false rule or claim and an execution. SKETCH
    31	identifies a proposed construction or a proof with a missing step. OPEN
    32	identifies an unsettled claim. In particular, a conditional timing formula
    33	does not prove that the protocol supplies its conditions.
