   116	For Q=⌈2n/3⌉, two quorums intersect in at least 2Q−n validators. With a≤f,
   117	2Q−n>a. The checkpoint-path argument therefore gives accountable safety
   118	for the fixed-set FG. This argument says nothing about the SA receipt
   119	cutoffs, lease map, or available-output P1.
   120	
   121	An FG-SA candidate could add an early available-output gate, a transfer
   122	phase, or an acknowledgement condition to FG votes. It might then use its
   123	justifications as persistent certificates. That is OPEN. The proof must
   124	establish the missing transfer property and all base claim domains. A rule
   125	that requires a PC to justify a checkpoint and then removes the PC service
   126	is circular. A rule that exposes J as the available output also loses the
   127	intended low-participation service: with n=10, a=1, h=2 and silent faults,
   128	SA can confirm 2/2 genuine support and slow-arm a prefix, but 2<Q=7.
   129	
   130	FG-PC-SA has the smaller first proof task. The two services have separate
   131	jobs: PCs provide timely committee evidence at slot scale; FG links provide
   132	cross-epoch finality. A PC adds a field to the HEAD duty, not a separate
   133	available ledger. Proving this composition first gives a reference against
   134	which a later FG-SA reduction can be checked.
