   581	
   582	**F advances.** A proper F advance has a larger finalized height:
   583	finalized checkpoints at an equal height are the same justified entry.
   584	Under this cap its height is at most m−1. Thus there are at most
   585	`m−1−f0` new aggregate F levels. Local readers can catch up to old
   586	levels as well. Their initial catch-up takes the same relay margin;
   587	it is not a new adversarial certificate.
   588	
   589	If `f_new≤m−2`, every band witness W extends F_new by [DC5]. A
   590	previous retained prefix B witnessed by W either precedes F_new, or
   591	remains witnessed above it. Such a finalization cannot exclude a band
   592	branch. If `f_new=m−1`, it supplies the unique top J and is charged
   593	to that same possible branch exclusion. Once Z=J at m−1, every later
   594	F under the cap precedes J or equals it; the predicate `F⪯B` is then
   595	redundant above Z.
   596	
   597	This proves at most one **branch-excluding** event. For N1's literal
   598	F-constancy premise, this file nevertheless counts every aggregate F
   599	advance and allows settling and repair after it. It does not need a
   600	stronger exact-service theorem through changing finality bases.
