## 61. Round 94 (2026-09-27): FG on SA — scope

Source: [codex/fg-sa-scope.md](codex/fg-sa-scope.md) (Astra, paper).

- PROVED: an FFG justification is not a PC (no receipt deadline, no HEAD
  extension), so it cannot replace the PC's transfer role as is.
- REFUTED: E1 r19 without its PC gate breaks SA P1; E2 base-first
  priority gives no bounded FG recovery; E3 the r19 deadline plus SA's
  2L does not bound the composition.
- Recommendation: FG-PC-SA first (frozen FG source, mandatory SA leases,
  a fresh PC checkpoint after recovery; SKETCH); FG-SA later as a
  reduction with an explicit replacement for PC transfer (OPEN). NJ
  heights not proved necessary; keep them as a fallback.
- MODEL GAP: strict C* has no validator identity across labels, so FFG
  slashing evidence (double vote, surround) is not expressible. Proposed:
  an additive fixed-identity authentication interface for full-set FG
  duties; available-chain duties stay strict C*.

## 62. Round 95 (2026-09-27): SA-PC improvements

Source: [codex/sapc-improve.md](codex/sapc-improve.md) (Astra, paper).

- PROVED: recovery needs only a ≤ f and h_t ≥ q (not full participation),
  same ρ = 2L+G+8Δ; PC service 6Δ at h_t ≥ q.
- REFUTED: unchanged SA-PC base recovers at every h > a. PROVED: a gate
  repair gives base recovery at h > a and h ≥ 2f (some cases above the
  cap). Full h > a base recovery with the strong bundle: OPEN.
- n/3: PROVED for arbitrary-prefix agreement or irrevocability; OPEN for
  persistence after healthy arming only. One lease: REFUTED for SA/SA-PC.

## 63. Round 97 (2026-09-27): simplex FG healing over SA / SA-PC

Source: [codex/fg-healing.md](codex/fg-healing.md) (Astra, paper). FG =
decoupled-consensus simplex FG (heights, grades, filter, NJ), full-set
identities; base SA or SA-PC.

- PROVED: how the decoupled protocol heals today (Lean): "instant
  assurance" is conditional — view merge gives common honest opening
  HEADs within one 6Δ slot once root and grade conditions hold.
- REFUTED: instant assurance with lease-bound FG sources: SA's slow-arming
  §7 run keeps honest groups on X/Y leases ~2L after GST, so honest round
  proposals get no common FG source; with SA-PC a withheld PC(C) keeps S
  on C and gives zero honest height-2 target votes. Finite reorgs shown;
  unbounded bouncing OPEN. Late PCs cannot restart SA-PC's delay (F4).
- NJ as is: removes a justification height, does not give a quiet 2L
  interval; bounded FG-SA recovery with unchanged NJ OPEN.
- Justification priority over leases: q_F − a honest votes do not imply
  that lease holders voted outside their lease; P1 above the cap needs a
  switch; OPEN. Direct proposal votes: REFUTED. Local silence as a healed
  signal: REFUTED.
- Recommended SKETCH: FG-SA with a certified NJ drain (FG promise quorum
  blocks new target quorums for ≥ 2L+G+8Δ, then a certified restart on a
  fresh source). PC not a substitute for FG certificates (and vice versa);
  PC only needed for unbounded persistence.
- Model: one engine, committee duties in C*, FG duties signed by fixed
  identities with an anti-slashing record; noninterference obligations.

## 64. Round 105 (2026-09-27): instant healing with a current-round PC

Source: [codex/instant-heal-check.md](codex/instant-heal-check.md) (Astra).
Rule FT: a non-timeout FG target vote in round j needs a resolved PC for
the round-j opening proposal, which must be the height entry itself.

- BREAKS: unconditional instant healing. A fresh PC is necessary but does
  not give a common FG source or signing permission (A2, B1); the literal
  rule can stall height progress forever (needs a timeout repair).
- BREAKS: "fresh PC blocks every adversarial justification in the 2L
  window" (§4.2: 81/145 honest split + 66 faulty HEADs give a current PC
  and a private justification on X, a branch the base later abandons).
- PROVED (REPAIRED): old-evidence barrier — once an honest opening entry P
  gets its first FT target quorum, no pre-opening FG evidence (withheld
  quorums, old justifications) can restart the cascade (fixed-identity
  quorum intersection 2q_F − n > a, E2 record).
- NJ and the height filter are still used by the existing proof; removing
  them is OPEN.
- Bounds: base handoff 2L+G+8Δ PROVED; conditional FG bound
  ρ_base + 4gRΔ + 9Δ given the §1.2 voting premises; full joint bound OPEN.

## 65. Round 104 (2026-09-27): can a fresh PC certify the FG restart?

Source: [codex/fg-fresh-pc.md](codex/fg-fresh-pc.md) (Astra).

- REFUTED: a timely current-round PC proves that SA-PC has healed. Its raw
  quorum can include base equivocators (they count for the PC, not for
  lease release or genuine support), so a conflicting mandatory lease can
  survive; a justification can form on a branch the base later abandons
  (same mechanism as §64). The first common timely PC is not an FG
  recovery boundary. A passive FG coupling can stall forever.
- PROVED: the PC at SA-PC's proved recovery handoff is safe from late PCs;
  simplex accountable safety transfers with fixed identities; the base
  claims are unchanged for a passive FG projection; a justified target
  has a PC ancestor.
- Recommendation: keep FG-PC-SA, the fresh-PC gate and the evidence
  freeze; prove a joint source-and-lease invariant; keep NJ and the height
  filter. The vote condition that closes the gap is r106's task.

## 66. Round 106 (2026-09-27): vote safety at height NJ+1

Source: [codex/nj-vote-safety.md](codex/nj-vote-safety.md) (Astra).
Property (user): at h* = NJ+1, with no FG interference, whatever an honest
validator votes for stays canonical.

- REFUTED: fresh PC(P) + P ⪯ own S (abandonment, r105 §4.2 variant).
- PROVED: fresh PC(P) + a live SA lease on the exact current-opening P
  (in practice a fast lease: ≥ ⌈n/2⌉ non-equivocating supporters) at the
  +6Δ vote ⇒ every honest HEAD extends P from then on (permanent base
  choice) and every honest S contains P by +10Δ. Closes r105 §4.2.
  Safe votes may happen before base recovery completes: no drain needed
  for vote safety.
- REFUTED: the same rule puts P in every S AT the vote time. PROVED: with
  a one-base-gate wait (vote at the next FG round), S-now safety holds.
- Slow lease: transfers when wholly synchronous, but not available for
  the current opening at +6Δ.
- OPEN: the full NJ recovery theorem and bound for the composition.

## 67. Round 108 (2026-09-27): full FG-PC-SA candidate

Source: [codex/fgpcsa-spec.md](codex/fgpcsa-spec.md) (Astra, 1527 lines).
Vote rule: PC + live lease on the exact current opening, after its gate.

- PROVED: T1 local lease invariants and E1/E2; T4 accountable finality
  (fixed identities); T5 finalized ⪯ strong ⪯ available by accessors; T6
  NJ arithmetic; T7 vote safety at NJ+1 (conditional); T8 two-lease
  handoff with noninterference; T9 conditional +6Δ target, +9Δ
  justification.
- OPEN: T2/T3 composite base and strong claims; T10 bounded NJ arrival and
  joint safe continuation (main obligation: a joint source and
  height-capture theorem).
- REFUTED T11: finality liveness with the strict current-opening target
  and the unchanged carrier inclusion — in a healthy all-honest run, every
  height entry lands at slot ≡ 2 mod R, never an opening, so after the
  first finalization only timeouts happen, forever. Needs a repair
  aligning height entries with openings (entry capture).
- Conditional bound: finalization ≤ GST + B_NJ(β) + 2L + G + 8Δ + 8gRΔ
  + 18Δ, given a proved height-progress lag β.

## 68. Round 110 (2026-09-27): opening entry capture; T10 deadlock

Source: [codex/entry-capture.md](codex/entry-capture.md) (Astra).

- PROVED: repair (a) — only an opening block can consume a height quorum,
  so every height entry is an opening. Healthy unanimous runs finalize
  every opening from round 2 by the next opening's +9Δ. T7 and the
  exact-entry old-evidence barrier unchanged.
- REFUTED T10 (and any finite joint bound) for r108's coupling, n = 4:
  before GST, U (2 honest) + faulty justify X legitimately (PC + fast
  lease at U only); the carrier C_X is withheld; the base moves to Y and
  heals before GST. After disclosure the FG domain is X-descendants while
  the base (mandatory leases, full honest support) stays on Y: no honest
  height or finality pair ever again; F = genesis forever.
- Cause: r108 gives SA leases priority over the FG root. Needed: a
  coupling repair that supplies progress in this split state (e.g. the
  decoupled-consensus rule "base follows the justified root", made
  P1-safe by the vote rule), without breaking base/strong claims. OPEN.

## 69. Round 112 (2026-09-27): FG root priority

Source: [codex/fg-root-priority.md](codex/fg-root-priority.md) (Astra).
Rule: the base follows the FG domain (finalized, justified root, height
filter), overriding SA leases; vote rule PC + fast lease; opening entries.

- PROVED: root priority resolves the §68 X/Y deadlock; a first
  conflicting justification is impossible before a first departure from
  a common protected prefix (the fast-lease vote rule works as expected).
- REFUTED (base safety, monotone, both P1s, 6Δ, strong persistence): a
  TIMEOUT quorum raises the height filter without any justification. n=4,
  a=1: honest FG duties skip action 30 while all base duties run (r108
  made committee and FG sleep independent); a faulty X gets G2 grades,
  the three honest validators time out (2,X), and a withheld timeout
  carrier later removes an armed B from the viable domain.
- Fix directions: one awake predicate per validator for all duties, and
  the simplex participation premises (awake-window majority, grade-forming
  majority) in the composite regimes; or keep the height filter from
  overriding protected leases. T10 still OPEN.

## 70. Round 124 (2026-09-28): one awake predicate, DC height filter

User decisions: one awake predicate for all duties; the decoupled height
filter and participation premises. The r112 attack needs an FG-only sleep
gap and is now excluded. A new attack remains. In an outage the simplex
grade window expires long before an SA lease or a PC. Faulty safe votes
can then make a local grade-2 source X that conflicts with the protected
B. Honest timeouts on X raise h_max twice, and the band removes B. The
live-lease veto on the height source stops this until the lease expires;
it does not protect the PC without expiry. Candidate (r125): a height
source must be compatible with the local PC and with every live lease.
Details: codex/fg-joint-sleep.md.

## 71. Round 125 (2026-09-28): PC-gated FG sources

Rule: a height source and a safe vote must be compatible with the
selected PC and with every live lease. This blocks both r124 attacks.
Band lemma: a carrier that raises h_max to m+1 extends the entry T_m.
Either T_m ⪯ B, and then height(B) ≥ m, or the carrier extends B and is
itself a witness. Two failures remain. (a) The live h_max cache can come
from a block outside the frozen HEAD view; the view then has no witness
for B. (b) The strict r106 recheck stops a repeated target, and a
finality lock stops the timeout; heights then stall after GST. Repairs
under test (r127): a band from the duty's own view, and a repeated
recorded target, as in decoupled consensus. Details: codex/fg-pc-source.md.

## 72. Round 126 (2026-09-28): SA-PC base recovery without the cap

The PC layer blocks base recovery through the live-PC veto on S writes:
a stale PC that cannot be replaced (h < q) rejects every conflicting
genuine result. Rule G_A: keep an unpruned archive of every PC; a write
with support > f passes as before; a lower-support write must be
compatible with every archived PC. Paper proof: base recovery at
h > max(a, f); at full participation this is every a < n/2 (bound
2L+2G+10Δ; 2L+G+8Δ under the cap). Clean base and capped strong claims
stay. Gap: a < h ≤ f (low participation under the cap); two archived
conflicting PCs then block forever. A PC expiry timer breaks no-expiry
persistence. Red-team r128; Lean rank 1 (h ≥ q) r129.
Details: codex/sapc-base-recovery.md.

## 73. Round 127 (2026-09-28): view band and repeated targets

R1: each duty computes h_max from its own view, and keeps every accepted
finalization. R2: a target that passed r106 earlier repeats without a
new r106 check. Both repairs stop the r125 traces. The retention and
clean claims are sketches; they need a port of the DC source-to-HEAD
proof. T10 fails again: a validator can get a finality lock on X with
no target record. The DC client then repeats the lock target, but r106
rejects it as a first target, and the lock forbids a timeout. Round 130
keeps the DC height_pair exactly, applies r106 only to fresh adoption,
and audits every DC progress lemma. Details: codex/fg-repairs.md.

## 74. Round 130 (2026-09-28): the DC client with a local PC check

R3: use the DC height_pair unchanged. Apply the r106 check only in the
fresh-adoption branch; if it fails, the DC timeout follows. A lock
repeat creates no new first quorum, so it is safe. R3 removes both
recorded-target stalls. An audit of the DC progress producer lists 28
obligations (A01–A28) for a Lean port. The next gap is in the proof,
not a stall: a gated safe vote can be empty, and a full honest batch of
empty votes forms no grade (A06, A07). Round 131 tests a clamp (the
deepest allowed ancestor instead of an empty value) and attempts the
T10 producer. Details: codex/fg-dc-client.md.

## 75. Round 131 (2026-09-28): clamp and the T10 producer

R4: when the PC gate rejects a safe value or a height source, use its
deepest allowed ancestor, not an empty value. Honest safe votes are then
never empty, and grade production works again. T10 is proved on paper
under one premise: the base has healed at GST+ρ for the actual mixed
duties. Then β = 6g+20 rounds, and the NJ boundary (or a finalization)
arrives by GST+ρ+P[3+(D+K+5)β]. Open: prove that premise for the mixed
duties (A24), and the healthy-prefix history (A25). Round 132 writes a
consolidated spec and attacks A24/A25; round 133 red-teams R1–R4.
Details: codex/fg-t10-producer.md.

## 76. Rounds 132–133 (2026-09-28): consolidated spec and red-team

codex/fgpcsa-v2.md Part 1 is now the reference FG-PC-SA rule set. The
red-team (r133) refuted nothing. Two negatives from r132: (a) a private
justification from before GST, disclosed after GST+ρ, moves the FG root
off the healed base, so the base handoff cannot be a continuing fact
from GST+ρ; (b) the public strong output (PC prefix on S) does not
persist from arming at T+Δ, because S takes the PC target at different
times at different readers. Plan (r134): recovery proof by frames
(the base heals inside a fixed frame; each frame change raises a bounded
potential), with the base handoff at height NJ+1, and an arming lag for
the strong output.

## 77. Round 134 (2026-09-28): frames and the recovery count

A potential on the duty frame fails: in one slot, a full-view proposal
and a frozen HEAD view can see different frames (A, B, A). The causal
cap holds (a carrier made only from old rows has height at most M+1),
but a post-GST carrier can reuse old target rows. In a common frame, the
next HEAD covers a synchronous genuine source (proved). An aggregate
potential m+j+f gives an explicit NJ bound, but it depends on the
initial frontier M and needs a settling lemma. At H+1 the root is F
(proved). Open: settling, exact proposal service, and history at NJ+1.
The strong output needs an arming lag of 4Δ in SA-PC (proved minimal).
Round 135 tries the three lemmas and a one-frame-per-slot rule (S1).

## 78. Round 135 (2026-09-28): settling and a uniform NJ bound

Keep the current rules; one frame per slot (S1) gives no shortcut.
Proved on paper: frames settle within P when no new evidence arrives; in
a common frame the base repairs within ρ; a lower-J disclosure or an F
change below the band does not remove a repaired path, and at most one
effective root change occurs per frontier. This gives a uniform bound
B_NJ = P[3+(D+K+5)(2⌈ρ/P⌉+12g+44)] for the NJ boundary. Open: O3, the
departure from NJ+1 by a timeout before the base repairs. Round 136 tests
the DC timeout delay δ_t ≥ ρ at NJ+1.

## 79. Round 136 (2026-09-28): timeout delay at NJ+1

R5(b): for an entry whose parent state has nj=true, a progress quorum is
consumed only after d·R slots, d = max(2, ⌈(ρ+2P+Δ)/P⌉). The rule is
local. It keeps the healthy latency and a uniform NJ bound. A long delay
at all heights (variant a) can stop finality forever. O3 stays open: an
honest H+1 timeout signed before the base repairs stays usable later.
Round 137 tests a signing-side wait (R6).

## 80. Round 137 (2026-09-28): signing delay at NJ+1

R6: an honest validator signs a timeout for an entry whose parent state
has nj=true only after its own frames have shown that height for
W = ρ+2P+Δ. Every honest H+1 timeout that leaves H+1 is then signed
after the base repairs, and the first H+2 band step keeps the repaired
block. Keep R5(b). The healthy latency does not change. Remaining: the
DC named-source history (same-round entry agreement, HEAD coverage,
later history) for the mixed walk, and the finalized arm of the NJ
consumer. Round 138 attempts both.

## 81. Round 138 (2026-09-28): named sources

Proved: after a seed interval both FG source arms are covered by the
first interior HEAD; a longer wait puts the seed before the first
timeout on the NJ arm; honest finality votes above the causal cap come
after the cut. Open: the full history fold of DC for the SA-PC walk
(one joint invariant, fg-named-source.md §4.3) and the repair on the
finalized arm. The R5(b)/R6 pseudocode is in fg-named-source.md §7.
Status: every FG attack so far is blocked; the recovery proof reduces to
these two ports.

